    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 521\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 7009, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to training\n      of fire officers in cities of one million or more\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would require that fire officers in New York City receive an\nadditional 80 hours of field and classroom training on the City's  fire,\nbuilding  and  construction  codes  as well as the applicable City ordi-\nnances.\n\n  The New York City Mayor's Office has urged me to disapprove this  bill\nfor  several  reasons,  including  the  significant fiscal impact of the\nbill.\n\n  I vetoed a similar bill in 2013 and expressed my  wish  that  the  new\nmayor  and New York City's unions would reach an agreement on the appro-\npriate scope of training. Although it appears that  differences  between\nthe parties remain, I am not prepared to dictate to the City the specif-\nics  of  its  training  programs, particularly when such programs have a\nsignificant fiscal impact.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n                              __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 521,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2014
   }
